the onyx logic introduction to  bioinformatics program  is an introduction to the field of  bioinformatics  or the intersection of informatics and  biology  in this program we will discuss the  changing landscape of data-driven  research and life sciences and the  opportunities that come  with the widely accessible high  throughput technologies  as well as computational methods for  analysis  and annotation of detailed data in  research and  industry we will discuss various data  types  emerging technologies as well as their  impact  on healthcare agriculture environmental  sciences  public health and more  in just six interactive sessions you  will get to see  the broad applications of next  generation sequencing  biostatistics as well as tools for big  data analysis  in practical assignments we will be  learning about the logic of  bioinformatics  to see how data science methods and  thinking can be used to study biology  in conclusion you will also be able to  plan how to take what you have learned  and apply it to an independent research  project using tools and methods  that we cover in the program preparing  biologists and clinicians for the influx  of data  associated methodologies and data-driven  research projects  is as prominent in biology as the  emergence of  computers for the tech industry more and  more biologists and clinicians are now  expected to both understand and handle  their own data  to publish and succeed in basic and  translational research projects  in fact biology itself is rapidly  acquiring the character of a data  science  billions of data points and genes  proteins and other molecules  are stored in large databases and should  be studied systematically  this program will give you a  comprehensive overview of bioinformatics  methods  and thinking for students biologists  and clinicians we will combine online  interactive sessions  self-guided study materials and  practical assignments for an immersive  experience  that has proven to be so effective in  the well-known  and respected onyx logic bioinformatics  training programs  the coursework that you will have access  to will provide you  with introductory materials that have  been taken  by thousands of people from all over the  world  online quizzes will cover important  terminology and provide  a perspective from experts on this  exciting field  each course will provide you with  important information  and will allow you to see how much you  have learned  all of this activity is going to be  measured using our unique  point system that lets us identify any  technical issues  and resolve roadblocks that are so  common for bioinformatics starters  at the end of the program each student  will receive  a personal certificate of participation  you will also experience our novel  project based approach  to learning bioinformatics we take data  sets  from high impact publications and use  the methods described there  to practice the analysis these projects  include such topics as oncology  neuroscience agriculture  and many others as a result anyone  starting on this journey of  bioinformatics  can start developing a project of their  own  by seeing how experts analyze their data  and achieve research results  you too can start developing a research  question of your own  and identify the appropriate type of  data and plan  the analysis using tools and skills that  you have  gained for the duration of the program  we will be using  the t bioinfo platform to process big  data sets  this platform is built for multi-omics  integration  and analysis of structured data with  advanced methods like machine learning  and mathematical modeling this  analytical platform will provide a  hands-on experience for anyone  without any technical prerequisites they  can apply  the advanced skills to interesting data  sets with color-coded logical maps  explanation of methods detailed input  and output formats  and reproducible workflows downstream  analysis and visualization of process  data  can be performed in popular coding  languages like  r and python so we will also offer an  introduction to several basic methods  and popular packages used in  bioinformatics  from visualization of genomic data to  exploratory analysis  and hypothesis testing to machine  learning  this course provides a broad overview  but it is structured to offer  significant depth  even for the experienced user after  completing the short introduction  you will be inspired to continue  learning about this exciting field  of bioinformatics as a result you will  learn about  important bioinformatics concepts and  applications  various applications of next generation  sequencing  the role of data science for biologists  and  industry challenges addressed by big  data  informatics the program will be guided  by highly experienced mentors with  doctorate degrees  in bioinformatics and computational  biology  dr harpreet kaur will guide the  interactive  sessions offering advice and training  based on her  own personal experience that she gained  in multiple research projects  that leverage big data for exciting  discoveries  onyx logic programs are a result of  close collaboration between pine biotech  an innovative big data analytics company  based in the us  and numerous academic institutions that  have participated  in content evaluation curriculum review  and project design as a result the omics  logic programs have been thoroughly  tested  and are known to lead to excellent  outcomes for students  and faculty interested in bioinformatics  data science  and biomedical research after you  complete the program  we will also offer you to continue with  us  as a research fellow  to summarize we welcome you to join this  program  and earn a certificate of excellence for  advanced projects  or a certificate of participation for  basic training  anyone without any technical background  can join this course and learn about the  emerging field  of big data bioinformatics
 

